## Troubleshooting CaDeT runner failures

If you see an error like below follow the troubleshooting steps outlined in this document. This error can occur when either a user or AWS terminates the spot compute that `karpenter` has assigned from AWS. The default position is that spot compute is consumed, this primarily is a cost saving decision. Spot compute should only be used for non-critical workloads that can be safely interrupted.

```text
The self-hosted runner lost communication with the server. Verify the machine is running and has a healthy network connection. Anything in your workflow that terminates the runner process, starves it for CPU/Memory, or blocks its network access can cause this error.
```

1. Examine the workflow in question to see if it's on spot or non-spot compute.

   a. **Spot:**

      i.

      ```text
      jobs:
        deploy:
          name: Deploy dbt project
          runs-on: [self-hosted, analytical-platform]
      ```

   b. **Non-spot:**

      i.

      ```text
      jobs:
        deploy:
          name: Deploy dbt project
          runs-on: [self-hosted, analytical-platform-non-spot]
      ```

2. If it's on spot compute follow these [steps to establish which spot instance was terminated](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/data-platform-support/issues/864).

3. Once you have this information examine the Dashboard in `analytical-platform-compute-production` here and establish the reason for the termination.
